WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.780
This is what a differential equation actually looks like. Every leaf is an answer.

2
00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:11.472
This has infinitely many answers. You only need two of them.

3
00:00:11.752 --> 00:00:13.192
- They're all just drifting.

4
00:00:13.472 --> 00:00:20.392
Pushed. Every point is a rule saying which way you go from there. That rule is a matrix.

5
00:00:20.671 --> 00:00:26.987
Drop a leaf anywhere and it curves. Drop a thousand. They all curve.

6
00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:30.425
Which is why guess and check is an embarrassment.

7
00:00:30.705 --> 00:00:32.238
Except here. And here.

8
00:00:32.517 --> 00:00:34.235
- Those two are going dead straight.

9
00:00:34.516 --> 00:00:40.460
On those two lines the matrix stops turning things. It only stretches them.

10
00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:46.917
And something that only stretches is not a matrix any more. It is a number.

11
00:00:47.197 --> 00:00:48.683
- The matrix becomes a number?

12
00:00:48.963 --> 00:01:00.248
On that one direction. A V equals lambda V. So X prime equals A X becomes X prime equals lambda X.

13
00:01:00.528 --> 00:01:05.311
Which you can solve in your sleep. E to the lambda T, times V.

14
00:01:05.591 --> 00:01:11.396
Two straight answers. And every other leaf in the field is just those two, mixed.

15
00:01:11.676 --> 00:01:22.822
Every solution the system will ever have, from two directions the wind cannot turn. Comment EIGEN and I'll send you the schematic.
